;; FH-ROOT-007 — the fallback, and its boundary.
;;
;; An empty container is not a near miss a hydration can reconcile. There is
;; no server render to adopt at all — the page was never server-rendered for
;; this root, or this root's region was composed in on the client — and
;; hydrating a non-empty client tree against nothing is a total divergence
;; React answers by discarding and re-rendering everything, loudly, for a
;; page that was never wrong.
;;
;; So `hydrate-root` recognises the one input it CAN recognise before React
;; is involved and mounts client-side instead, reporting it as the mount
;; kind rather than as N adoption errors. The page comes up correct either
;; way; what changes is whether the reader is handed a pile of diagnostics
;; about a page that was never server-rendered.
;;
;; The boundary is the other half of the row, and it is the part that could
;; quietly go wrong. A container carrying markup that merely DISAGREES is a
;; real hydration with a real mismatch — falling back there would throw away
;; the adoption the server render was paid for on the strength of one wrong
;; character, and would hide the disagreement while doing it.
;; MANIFEST PRESENCE IS THE SERVER-RENDER EVIDENCE, not a non-empty
;; container. A declared view may render nothing (an empty
;; `re-frame.freehand.tree-views/nothing`), so the server can emit an empty
;; container that still carries its Root Manifest — an empty SERVER render,
;; adopted under the manifest's identity (FH-ROOT-006), which is how
;; `hydrated?` tells it apart from a client-only load. The FALLBACK is
;; taken when NO manifest is adjacent: a page the server never rendered
;; emits neither markup nor a manifest, so the empty container with nothing
;; beside it comes up under the DERIVED identity an ordinary mount would
;; give it, and asks for no SSR artefact. Only a container that DOES carry
;; server markup, with nothing adjacent, is the broken-render failure.
{:fh/id "FH-ROOT-007"
 :fh/law
 "Manifest PRESENCE, not a non-empty container, is a hydrating root's server-render evidence: an empty container the server emitted for a view that rendered nothing still carries its Root Manifest and is ADOPTED under that identity, while a container with NO manifest adjacent takes the FALLBACK when it is empty — an ordinary client mount under the DERIVED identity, reported as the mount kind rather than as adoption errors and asking for no SSR artefact — and a container carrying markup that merely disagrees stays on the adoption path, reads its identity from the manifest, and takes the mismatch."

 :view  :greeting
 :props {:name "world"}

 ;; The fallback: an empty container, with NO manifest beside it — the
 ;; state a client-only first load is actually in. The root comes up,
 ;; correct, says it did not hydrate, and carries the derived identity.
 :empty-container {:hydrated false
                   :text     "world"
                   :mismatches 0
                   :manifest-present false
                   :root-id    :re-frame.freehand.root-views/greeting
                   :provenance :derived}

 ;; The empty SERVER render, and the point of the correction: a declared
 ;; view rendered nothing, so the container is empty — but the server
 ;; emitted its Root Manifest beside it all the same. Manifest PRESENCE is
 ;; what proves this empty DOM is a server render rather than a client-only
 ;; first load, so it ADOPTS under the manifest's identity instead of
 ;; falling back. The id and prefix are ones the nil-rooted view's OWN
 ;; derivation would never produce, so a passing assertion can only have
 ;; read them off the wire — never derived them and never planted them.
 :empty-server-render {:derived-root-id :re-frame.freehand.tree-views/nothing
                       :manifest {:rf.root/schema-version 1
                                  :root-id           :fh.root/empty-from-the-wire
                                  :identifier-prefix "empty-srv-"}
                       :root-id    :fh.root/empty-from-the-wire
                       :identifier-prefix "empty-srv-"
                       :provenance :manifest
                       :hydrated   true}

 ;; Whitespace-only is the same case — a formatted page skeleton is empty.
 :whitespace-container {:html "\n  " :hydrated false}

 ;; The boundary: markup that DISAGREES is still a hydration — so it still
 ;; reads its identity from the manifest beside it.
 :divergent-container
 {:html "<section id=\"greeting\"><h1 id=\"title\">Hello</h1><p id=\"who\">stale</p></section>"
  :manifest {:rf.root/schema-version 1
             :root-id           :fh.root/still-a-hydration
             :identifier-prefix "srv7-"}
  :root-id  :fh.root/still-a-hydration
  :hydrated true
  :mismatches-at-least 1
  :final-text "world"}

 ;; The fallback root is an ordinary root in every other respect: it holds
 ;; the same claims and tears down the same way.
 :live-roots-after-fallback 1
 :live-roots-after-unmount  0}
